## 🤔 What Does "Inspect HTML" Mean?

Every webpage you see in your browser is built using **HTML**.

Your browser renders the HTML into the webpage you see, but you can also view the underlying source code.

> 🧠 **Analogy:** Think of a webpage like a cooked dish 🍕. You see the pizza, but the **recipe** is hidden in the kitchen. Inspecting HTML is like going into the kitchen to read the recipe.

### Two Ways to View HTML

| Method                  | How                                                           |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 📄 **View Page Source** | Right-click → **View Page Source** or press `Ctrl + U`        |
| 🛠️ **Inspect Element** | Right-click → **Inspect** or press `F12` / `Ctrl + Shift + I` |

> 💡 **Difference:** "View Source" shows the raw HTML sent by the server, while "Inspect Element" shows the current DOM, which may have been modified by JavaScript.

For this challenge, **View Page Source** is the simplest approach.

