# 🔑 Step 2 — View the Source

Right-click anywhere on the page and select:

```text
View Page Source
```

Or press:

```text
Ctrl + U
```

A new tab will open containing the **raw HTML source code**.

It may look something like:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>...</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <h1>Welcome!</h1>
    <p>Some text here...</p>

    <!-- picoCTF{1n5p3t0r_0f_h7ml_XXXXXXXX} -->

    <p>More text...</p>
  </body>
</html>
```

🎉 The flag is hidden inside an **HTML comment**.

---

# 🤔 What's an HTML Comment?

An HTML comment looks like this:

```html
<!-- This is a comment. Browsers don't display it. -->
```

### Important Points

* `<!--` starts the comment.
* `-->` ends the comment.
* Browsers don't display the comment on the webpage.
* The comment is still included in the HTML source.
* Anyone who can view the source can read it.

> 🧠 **Analogy:** It's like a sticky note 📝 attached to the back of a poster. Visitors see the poster, but if they flip it around, they can read the note.

